<!-- M-ROKU-17 (review roku__gameux M2): the toast overlay, re-based onto
     Roku's built-in Dialog node class. The pre-fix markup extended Scene,
     which can never display: a Scene is not a legal Scene.dialog payload
     (Roku's Scene reference: "setting this field to a node extended from a
     Dialog node causes the dialog to be displayed"), the show write targeted
     a fabricated ComponentController node, and the dismiss path wrote
     m.top.close - the built-in Dialog's write-only dismiss control, not a
     Scene field. As a Dialog subclass this node displays by the estate's
     shipped dialog idiom (the PhlixApp root coordinator assigns it to the
     current surface's dialog field), is dismissed by the documented close
     control, and reports its exit via wasClosed; dialogs consume Back/Home
     natively, so no key handling ships here. The notice text rides the
     inherited title field (the only mandatory Dialog region) from the
     caller's copy, so this markup ships no user-facing literals and stays
     outside the CHECK25 translate net (its stale "Toast text here" EXEMPT
     entry rotated out with the label). -->
<component name="ToastScene" extends="Dialog">
</component>
